0..85 Comment "// Two programs exchange a ping over `std.net.Eff`, the host interface for streams to"
86..115 Comment "// peers named by their keys."
116..118 Comment "//"
119..194 Comment "// One process serves and another pings it, the first step from one process"
195..268 Comment "// to programs that coordinate across hosts. The same `ping` runs under a"
269..326 Comment "// handler written here, a second model of the interface."
327..329 Comment "//"
330..406 Comment "// `gandr run ping.gandr` serves, and `gandr run ping.gandr <key>@<ip:port>`"
407..480 Comment "// dials the server that key and socket name, then prints its answer. The"
481..564 Comment "// host binds its network on the run\'s first `std.net.Eff` operation, at the socket"
565..627 Comment "// `--net-bind` names, under the key `GANDR_NET_SECRET` holds."
628..630 Comment "//"
631..699 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-driver/tests/net.rs` — the two processes"
700..771 Comment "// - see: `crates/runtime-net/README.md` — the network the host binds"
773..800 Comment "// The native finite lists."
